IMPORT prelude

-- Family Provision Act 1970 (NT) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Built-in date functions only (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library.
-- The Act counts one period, twice: "within a period of 12 months after the date on which administration in respect of
-- the estate of the deceased person has been granted" (s 9(1)) and "within 12 months after the date on which
-- administration was granted" (s 20(1)).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Not an official version of the Family Provision Act 1970 (NT). Copyright in Northern Territory legislation
-- is owned by the Northern Territory. Quoted under the Northern Territory copyright policy of 8 October 1996; see
-- SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Family Provision Act 1970`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `falls before` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the first day` `falls after` `the second day` IF DATE_SERIAL `the first day` GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL `the second day`

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The number of days in a month of a year.
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `in` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- "Within 12 months after" day D: the day of the grant is excluded, so the period ends at the end of the same day of the
-- same month a year later, the last day on which an application is in time. A grant on 29 February ends on 28 February
-- (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day 12 months after` `the start` MEANS
    DATE_FROM_DMY (min (DATE_DAY `the start`) (`the length of month` (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `in` `the next year`)) (DATE_MONTH `the start`) `the next year`
    WHERE
        `the next year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the start` PLUS 1
